{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8f879536012842e8ddc896470e33cfa63fca6e6aa9baaef0d4065f2f38e176c7","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar CLI comment command","key_entities":["rebar comment","--body-file","--body","Usage: rebar comment <ticket_id> <body>","create","edit","session-log","tag","untag","archive","set-verify-commands","args[:min_args]"],"problem_keywords":["silent data loss","cli parsing","positional argument","flag collision","exit code 0","durability"],"propositions":["rebar comment silently stores flag-like tokens (--body-file, --body) as the comment body instead of rejecting them, causing intended content to be lost while exiting 0","the loss goes undetected because a comment record is created with the flag string, making len(comments) checks pass while the actual content is discarded","the same footgun affects multiple positional-body commands (create, edit, session-log) and requires a guard across all of them","users who attempt the intuitive --body-file or --body syntax lose their work durably with no error signal, contradicting rebar's documented guidance that the ticket store is the durable trail"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787887608416554001,"uuid":"98edfb0d-1531-4a6c-862a-76da55699e29"}